   "source": [
    "# ClauseGuard: Research Notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Introduction\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates the research and development of ClauseGuard, an explainable NLP framework for semantic-preservation verification in legal contract simplification. We adhere strictly to traditional NLP methods (no LLMs).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Base Research Paper Differentiation\n",
    "**Base Paper:** *Legal lay summarization: exploring methods and data generation with large language models* (Moro et al., 2026. DOI: 10.1007/s10462-025-11392-7).\n",
    "\n",
    "Unlike the base paper which relies heavily on LLMs, this project explores a simpler NON-LLM approach to:\n",
    "1. Legal document simplification\n",
    "2. Education-level-based explanation\n",
    "3. Legal terminology explanation\n",
    "4. Semantic preservation verification\n",
    "5. Automatic correction of detected meaning changes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Dataset & 3. Dataset Health\n",
    "We use a subset of the LEDGAR dataset for clause classification."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    df = pd.read_csv('../data/raw/dataset.csv')\n",
    "    print(f\"Loaded {len(df)} samples.\")\n",
    "    print(\"Class distribution:\", df['category'].value_counts().to_dict())\n",
    "except FileNotFoundError:\n",
    "    print(\"Dataset not found. Run scripts/fetch_dataset.py\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Preprocessing & Feature Extraction\n",
    "Cleaning and splitting into clauses, while preserving legal keywords."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "import os\n",
    "sys.path.append(os.path.abspath('..'))\n",
    "from src.preprocessing import preprocess_contract\n",
    "\n",
    "sample_text = \"The Supplier shall deliver the goods within 15 days; provided that the Purchaser pays $10,000.\"\n",
    "print(\"Clauses:\", preprocess_contract(sample_text))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Non-LLM Summarization\n",
    "Extractive summarization using TF-IDF sentence scoring."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from src.summarizer import summarize_text_extractive\n",
    "\n",
    "text_to_summarize = \"The Supplier shall deliver the goods. This is a very long and boring sentence that doesn't mean much. The Purchaser will pay the Supplier $10,000.\"\n",
    "print(\"Summary:\", summarize_text_extractive(text_to_summarize, num_sentences=2))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Education-Level Simplification & Legal Dictionary\n",
    "Simplifying based on user's reading level (Beginner, Intermediate, Advanced)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from src.simplifier import simplify_clause\n",
    "from src.legal_terms import detect_legal_terms\n",
    "\n",
    "clause = \"The Supplier shall indemnify the Purchaser aforementioned.\"\n",
    "print(\"Beginner:\", simplify_clause(clause, \"Beginner\"))\n",
    "print(\"Advanced:\", simplify_clause(clause, \"Advanced\"))\n",
    "print(\"Detected Terms:\", detect_legal_terms(clause))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Legal Information Extraction & 8. Preservation Checker\n",
    "Extracting actor, action, modality, dates, amounts, and verifying preservation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from src.preservation_checker_checker import check_preservation\n",
    "\n",
    "orig = \"The Supplier shall deliver the goods within 15 days.\"\n",
    "simp = \"The Supplier may deliver the goods within 30 days.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "report = check_preservation(orig, simp)\n",
    "print(f\"Risk Level: {report['risk_level']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Changed: {report['changed']}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Automatic Correction Loop\n",
    "If meaning changes, we automatically back off to a safer education level."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "clause = \"The Supplier shall deliver the goods.\"\n",
    "# Beginner simplification changes 'shall' to 'must'. This is low risk.\n",
    "simp_beginner = simplify_clause(clause, \"Beginner\")\n",
    "print(\"Beginner Simp:\", simp_beginner, \"-> Risk:\", check_preservation(clause, simp_beginner)['risk_level'])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Conclusion\n",
    "We successfully demonstrated an explainable, LLM-free NLP framework for preserving legal meaning during simplification, addressing the core research question."
   ]
  }
 ],
